The attached image, corresponding to Figure 2A and 2B in the PDF, illustrates the physical characterization of Nano-11 nanoparticles. Figure 2A, a Transmission Electron Microscopy (TEM) image, reveals spherical particles with an irregular, cauliflower-like appearance, showing single particles and occasional pairs, with a scale bar of 50 nm. Figure 2B, a dynamic light scattering (DLS) plot, indicates that the nanoparticles have a Z-average hydrodynamic diameter ranging from 75 to 80 nm, with a fairly uniform size distribution between 30 and 110 nm. These characteristics are important for efficient uptake by dendritic cells, contributing to their efficacy as vaccine adjuvants.